# =========================================================================================
# PART B — VERDICT `Reached`, and the census is the more informative half
# =========================================================================================
#
#   CONTROL OBSERVATION: daemon pgid 30007, ai comm "sai", 20 samples
#     matched in the daemon's group: [(30095, 'S', "sai")]
#     census: [(30010, 'S', "delphi-runtimed"), (30095, 'S', "sai"), (30098, 'R', "unix_chkpwd")]
#     verdict: Reached
#
# `Reached` is the first of the four outcomes named in the expectation. The scanner found the
# AI **alive** (`S`), verified as this daemon's child, across 20 samples — provenance and
# liveness, not a name match, which is what R34-01/02 forced.
#
# **THE CENSUS IS ITS OWN SMALL CONTROL.** It returns THREE processes, not just the target:
# a second `delphi-runtimed` (30010 — the leader 30007 is excluded by design, so this is the
# forked child before/at `execve`) and `unix_chkpwd` in state **R**, the PAM helper caught
# mid-authentication. **A scanner that only ever returned its own target would be
# indistinguishable from one matching on name alone**; this one enumerates the group and
# reports what is there. That distinction is not something the `Reached` verdict alone shows.
#
# What `Reached` does and does not buy, fixed in the expectation BEFORE the run: the
# supplementary scan is meaningful **for this run**. It does not touch the §4 closure either
# way — that rests on `killed == false` against a stubborn AI, observed independently of the
# scan. Reaping is still not independently observed.
#
# =========================================================================================
# ONE PROCESS DEFECT — a step that appears to run and does not
# =========================================================================================
#
# `$LOG`/`$STATUS` were unset in a fresh shell, so `: > ""` failed with
# `bash: : No such file or directory` and the chain stopped — **while looking like the
# long-running loop it was supposed to start.** Nothing was lost (the step was re-run), but the
# shape is the one this arc keeps paying for and is the SAME CLASS as run 20's dropped §4b: a
# check that presents as executed and was not. The procedure's own commands did not guard their
# variables; they now use `${VAR:?}`, which names the missing variable instead of failing at a
# token.
#
# Recorded because the failure was loud THIS time by luck of where it landed. `: > ""` happened
# to be the first command in the chain; the same unset variable inside the loop would have
# written a log nobody could find and produced a count from a stale file.
#
